What is Pest Control?

Pest Control refers to the management and regulation of species that are harmful to human health, property, agriculture, or the environment. This involves a combination of chemical, biological, mechanical, and increasingly digital methods to monitor, prevent, and eliminate pest populations such as rodents, insects, termites, and other invasive species. The industry has seen a notable shift toward sustainable practices as awareness of the environmental and health impacts of traditional pesticides continues to grow.

